// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO4-9 (LCD), GPIO10 (RFID IRQ), GPIO11/12
// (internal touch/RTC I2C bus), GPIO14 (touch interrupt), GPIO40/41
// (rotary encoder), GPIO46 (power-hold) - confirmed via M5Unified
// library source + official M5Stack docs.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO42 tagged "button" - confirmed physical front push
// button (below M5 logo, M5Dial.BtnA / M5Unified Button_Class), distinct
// from the rotary encoder A/B lines (G40/G41). Source: docs.m5stack.com
// M5Dial button page + M5Stack community thread confirming GPIO42 wiring.
